  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Some customers in a pizzeria were asked about the type of pizza they prefer between spicy pizza and vegetarian pizza. The results of the survey are summarized in the two-way frequency table below.\n\n|  | Prefers Spicy | Prefers  Vegetarian | Totals |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Children | $10$ | $22$ | $32$ |\n| Adults | $41$ | $27$ | $68$ |\n| Totals | $51$ | $49$ | $100$ |\n\nEstimate the probability that a randomly chosen person is an adult or prefers spicy pizza (or both).",
  "worked_solution": "To estimate the probability that a randomly chosen person is an adult or prefers spicy pizza, we\n\n- add up the numbers in the row **\"Adults\"** or the column **\"Prefers Spicy\"**, and\n\n- divide by the total number of data points in the table.\n\nThe numbers in the row **\"Adults\"** or the column **\"Prefers Spicy\"** are highlighted below.\n\n|  | Prefers Spicy | Prefers Vegetarian | Totals |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Children | $10$ | $22$ | $32$ |\n| Adults | $41$ | $27$ | $68$ |\n| Totals | $51$ | $49$ | $100$ |\n\nAdding up these numbers and then dividing by the total number of data points in the table $(100),$ we get\n\n$$\np=\\frac{10+41+27}{100}=\\frac{78}{100}=0.78.\n$$",
